        "findings": "VERDICT: CHANGES REQUESTED\n\nThe `AssignCustomerCode` logic itself lives in the right unit, but two structural/coherence issues:\n\n1. **Duplicated transformation in `AssignCustomerCode.service`.** `city3` and `last3` are now computed with the identical expression `x.substring(0, Math.min(3, x.length())).toUpperCase(Locale.ROOT)`. With the change this pattern appears twice verbatim. Extract a small private helper (e.g. `firstThreeUpper(String)`) so both derivations read the same and the \"first three, upper-cased\" rule has a single home.\n\n2. **Stale example in the derived value's Javadoc.** The spec says everything derived from `customerCode` \u2014 notably the membership number \u2014 must be rebuilt on the new format, and the diff duly updated the openapi example to `TOW-SMI-0007-M26`. But the equivalent example in `Owner.getMembershipNumber()`'s Javadoc (`src/main/java/.../model/Owner.java:154`) still reads `SMI-0007-M26`, the old format. The membership number concatenates `customerCode`, so the runtime value rebuilds automatically, but leaving the Java doc example on the old format while the openapi example moved to the new one is exactly the kind of incoherence a maintainer trips over. Update the Javadoc example to the new format for consistency."
